@startuml

'skinparam ClassBorderColor #F1C40F
skinparam ClassBorderColor #D4AC0D
skinparam stereotypeABorderColor #A9DCDF
skinparam stereotypeIBorderColor #B4A7E5
skinparam stereotypeCBorderColor #ADD1B2
skinparam stereotypeEBorderColor #EB93DF
skinparam shadowing false

skinparam StateBorderColor #D4AC0D
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #D4AC0D

' Red
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor<<red>> #FDEDEC
skinparam ClassBorderColor<<red>> #E74C3C
hide <<red>> stereotype
' Purple
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor<<purple>> #F4ECF7
skinparam ClassBorderColor<<purple>> #8E44AD
hide <<purple>> stereotype
' blue
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor<<blue>> #EBF5FB
skinparam ClassBorderColor<<blue>> #3498DB
hide <<blue>> stereotype
' Green
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor<<green>> #EAFAF1
skinparam ClassBorderColor<<green>> #2ECC71
hide <<green>> stereotype

' Orange
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor<<orange>> #FDF2E9
skinparam ClassBorderColor<<orange>> #E67E22
hide <<orange>> stereotype

' Grey
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor<<grey>> #EAECEE
skinparam ClassBorderColor<<grey>> #2C3E50
hide <<grey>> stereotype

actor "Ticketing Application" as app #gold
participant "Calypso\nCard API" as capi #pink
participant "Reader API" as rapi #pink
participant "Calypso Card\nReader" as cardReader #lightBlue
boundary "**Card**" as card #lightBlue

activate app #gold

== Parallel selection of several applications ==

note over capi
    Two applications of the same card are targeted.
    The card must support several logical channels in parallel.
end note

app->capi: <font color=red>**prepare**</font> card selection:\n\t- filter by AID #1
activate capi  #pink
capi-->app
deactivate capi

app->capi: <font color=red>**prepare**</font> card selection:\n\t- filter by AID #2
activate capi  #pink
capi-->app
deactivate capi

app->rapi: <font color=red>**prepare**</font> card selection scenario:\n\t- selection case #1\n\t- selection case #2
activate rapi  #pink
rapi-->app
deactivate rapi

app->rapi: <font color=red>**process**</font> the selection scenario for\n**several applications in parallel**\n(one logical channel each)
activate rapi  #pink

rapi-[#0000FF]>cardReader: <font color=blue>**Card #1**</font>\ntransmit selection request\n\t- card selectors\n\t- APDU list
activate cardReader #lightBlue

cardReader->card: open card channel
activate card #lightBlue
card-->cardReader
cardReader->card: select application (aid #1) on the basic channel
card-->cardReader: [card FCI #1]
cardReader->card: open an additional logical channel
card-->cardReader: [channel reference]
cardReader->card: select application (aid #2) on that channel
card-->cardReader: [card FCI #2]

cardReader--[#0000FF]>rapi: receive selection response
deactivate cardReader

rapi-->app: [selection result:\n\t- card image of application #1, on the basic channel\n\t- card image of application #2, on its own channel\n\tboth active in parallel]
deactivate rapi

== Transaction on each application ==

app->app: **start** a card transaction on **application #1**:\n\t- secured with a **symmetric** crypto module\n\t- in **regular** mode, with its security settings

app->capi: <font color=red>**prepare**</font> card transaction:\n\t- read contract list
activate capi  #pink
capi-->app
deactivate capi

app->capi: <font color=red>**process**</font> commands
activate capi  #pink
capi-[#0000FF]>cardReader: <font color=blue>**Card #2**</font>\ntransmit card request\n\t- APDU list
activate cardReader #lightBlue
cardReader->card: read record (contract list) on the basic channel
card-->cardReader: [contract list data]
cardReader--[#0000FF]>capi: [contract list data]
deactivate cardReader
capi-->app: [card image of application #1 (updated)]
deactivate capi

note over app
    The other application stays active meanwhile:
    no new selection is needed to come back to it.
end note

app->app: **start** a card transaction on **application #2**:\n\t- **free**, no crypto module

app->capi: <font color=red>**prepare**</font> card transaction:\n\t- read event log
activate capi  #pink
capi-->app
deactivate capi

app->capi: <font color=red>**process**</font> commands **and close** the logical channel
activate capi  #pink
capi-[#0000FF]>cardReader: <font color=blue>**Card #3**</font>\ntransmit card request\n\t- APDU list
activate cardReader #lightBlue
cardReader->card: read record (event log) on the additional channel
card-->cardReader: [event log data]
cardReader->card: close that logical channel
card-->cardReader: ack
deactivate card
cardReader--[#0000FF]>capi: [event log data]
deactivate cardReader
capi-->app: [card image of application #2 (updated)]
deactivate capi

note over app
    Closing a logical channel deactivates the matching card image only.
    The application selected on the basic channel remains usable.
end note

@enduml
